   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to reporting on handgun licenses",
    "basePrintNo": "S7953",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7953-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §837-s, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7953\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the executive law, in relation to reporting on handgun licenses\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo require the Division of Criminal Justice\nServices to\nreport on the administration of certain laws related to handgun\nlicenses.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 of the bill amends the executive law\nby adding a new section 837-s to require an annual report by the\nDivision of Criminal Justice Services on the administration, function\nand effectiveness of administration of the laws regarding the\nissuance, modification of, amendment to, and revocation of handgun\nlicenses in each city with a population greater than one million and\neach county. The report shall include a description of how\napplications for handgun licenses are received, processed, reviewed,\nand approved or rejected;\ninformation on personnel and staffing employed to process and\nadminister handgun licenses; for each of the preceding five calendar\nyears, the number of handgun licenses issued, the number of handgun\nlicenses revoked, the number of handgun licenses amended, the number\nof applications for handgun licenses rejected, and the number of\nhandgun licenses outstanding at the end of the year; and a detailed\ndescription of instruction, if any, offered to handgun license\napplicants or licensees.\n\nSection 2 of the bill sets forth the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe State Police currently maintains a\nmaster database\nof all records of handgun transactions and pistol license issuances,\namendments cancellations, and revocations throughout the State, a\nrepository for the mandated \"records of transaction\" that\naccompany sales by gun dealers or between private residents. This\ninformation helps the State Police quickly establish the current\nownership of a weapon and the legality of a person's possession\nof a weapon.  This bill would build on the efforts already in place\nto accumulate this data by requiring the Division of Criminal\nJustice to submit an annual report to the legislature and the\nGovernor that presents  statistical information based on this data\non a county by county basis.  The bill would also provide a useful\ndescription of the handgun licensing policies and procedures\nfollowed by each issuing authority throughout the State.  Both\nthe statistics and the overview of policies and procedures\n\nwould increase transparency and provide a helpful backdrop for\npolicy discussions among legislators and the public at large.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nThis is a new bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE:\nMinimal.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
